WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:02.800
Hey Youtubers, it's Charlie

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:06.640
So huge news, George R.R. Martin was at a convention this past weekend and read from new

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:07.800
material from "Winds of Winter".

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:13.100
So he revealed some big details about Briennes backstory that made her that much more badass.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:16.580
So, just careful for spoilers if you don't want to know anything about Brienne.

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:20.860
Brienne is one of those characters that's been really put upon as she tells her history.

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:26.820
There was an episode where she was talking to Pod  explaining how they called her, "Brienne the Beauty", as an insult.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:30.500
Because even though you look at her right now and she's really big, really strong, total badass

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:36.680
You have to remember that she's probably been that tall since she was about 15 or 16, maybe even younger than that.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:43.420
It takes boys just a little big longer to catch up at that age, so if you think she's taller than say like Ser Jaime now

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:46.600
than imagine how big the difference was when they were teenagers.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:53.960
So as she tells it, as a child her father tried to marry her off 3 times just like you would a traditional lady from a noble house

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:58.060
but it led to 3 broken engagements just because no one would have her.

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:03.120
... and you could imagine how bad things got when she would just embarrass people that would get into fights with her.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:07.220
Like she'd spar with some of the other nobles and just kick their asses

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:13.600
So you could imagine like all those young noble boys wounded pride just saying awful awful things about her, her entire life.

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.380
So as much as that sucks, she's become this amazing badass on the TV show.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:21.560
She's still a badass in the books, the show has just pushed her to the forefront a little bit more.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:23.340
She's a little bit more of a background character in the books.

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:27.000
But here's the really cool thing that George R.R. Martin did this past weekend:

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:34.520
If you've read the Dunc and Egg series, Ser Duncan the Tall is named the protector of young Egg, Aegon the Fifth

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:36.380
who becomes the future King of Westeros.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:44.300
So that series is all about their adventures together like this really giant hedge knight and the future King of Westeros just palling around over the Seven Kingdoms.

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:50.060
But of the new material George R.R. Martin read, he named Brienne the descendant of Ser Duncan the Tall.

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:57.120
So just a really easy fix to make a character that everyone already loves that has a pretty terrible backstory, have a really amazing backstory.

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:01.140
Oh, like you think she had it bad but she comes from this amazing lineage.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:03.500
So just think of all the amazing things she's gonna do.

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:05.180
Hopefully she makes it to season 8.

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:08.160
She's one of those characters that definitely throws herself in the line of fire.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:13.680
So given that we have several characters now that all have Valyrian swords, including the newest, Samwell.

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:19.900
It would be such a disappointment if she didn't get to use Oathkeeper at some point to just Hulk out on some White Walkers.

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:24.600
But let me know in the comments what do you think about Brienne being the descendant of Ser Duncan the Tall.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:30.940
If you haven't read the books, he's kind of like the most famous knight in the history of Westeros. At least at this point.

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:32.900
The show has actually invoked a little bit of Dunc and Egg.

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:37.640
You may have missed it briefly but Maester Aemon talks about Egg as he's dying.

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:40.580
"Egg, Egg mothers calling you."

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:48.020
Egg, from the Dunc and Egg series was one of Maester Aemons brothers. You have to remember, Maester Aemon is very very old.

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:51.100
It was a really touching, sweet moment.

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:57.860
Especially what happened to his family later in life. At the end of his life that King Aegon died in what was called the Tragedy at Summerhall.

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:05.120
Side note: It's actually one of the instances that people point to when they say that Targaryens, not all Targaryens are immune to fire.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:09.420
Because they died in a giant house fire. Like almost his entire family was wiped out.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:18.780
The really cool thing about Dunc and Egg is that George R.R. Martin has actually pointed to it as his leading choice for a spinoff should HBO decide to do a Game of Thrones spinoff.

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:23.820
I think they definitely want to, but Dan and Dave are so set on finishing what they're doing right now...

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:29.120
... getting through the next season that they haven't announced anything about a spinoff yet, whether it's going to have different producers...

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:33.900
... but George R.R. Martin is like, "full steam ahead" he's like two thumbs up definitely go for it, do a spinoff.

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:38.380
So if we get a spinoff it will probably be the adventures of Dunc and Egg.

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:41.300
George R.R. Martin said that he's going to continue to write Dunc and Egg.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:45.600
He'll continue to write expanded material. So there will be plenty more new awesome people that he introduces

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:51.280
But as of right now it's just that Ser Duncan the Tall is the perfect ideal of the person that Brienne is trying to become.

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:54.080
All I ever wanted to do was become a knight she says.

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:57.720
That's why I've been a little dissapointed with Jaime  this season so far.

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:02.540
Yeah, he's been on a tear, we got to see that amazing Mad King, Kingslayer flashback.

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:08.120
But I think it's especially disappointing for book readers because in the books he's on a slightly more redemptive arc.

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:16.740
In the show, thus far, at least this far in the season up to episode 6 makes it seem like he's learned nothing-- like none of Briennes good qualities have rubbed off on him.

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:22.880
That's why I'm just waiting for someone to write fan-fiction where Tormund and Jaime fight for Briennes affections.

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:30.060
But remember Brienne will eventually head down to the Riverlands to try and secure the help of the Blackfish in Sansas quest to retake Winterfell.

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:35.600
Jaime is being sent to the Riverlands at the head of the Lannister Army to try and get rid of the Blackfish.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:37.800
So they will definitely be meeting up with each other

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:47.260
... and for those of you that are wondering where Bronn is, he actually appears in the trailer briefly here putting Pod in a choke-hold like, "Oh my god I can't believe I haven't seen you in so long."

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:56.220
So Bronn is still around it's just that Jaime only just mentioned him in the previous episode when he was like I'm going to get Bronn, we're going to assassinate the High Sparrow...

